# Portal local development

- Run the Portal with `dotnet run --project Api --launch-profile http`; the app is at `http://localhost:5000`.
- Build the SPA before expecting UI changes: `cd Web && npm run build` (output is `Api/wwwroot`). Re-run it after every Web change; the API does not hot-reload the SPA.
- Do not use Docker Compose locally. It is CI/prod scaffolding and will not match the local Okta and SQL setup (`127.0.0.1,1434` / `127.0.0.1,1435`).
- Quick compile check after C# edits: `dotnet build Api -c Debug`. Warning count must not grow.
- `cd Web && npm run test:ci` exits 1 on `main` (pre-existing). Do not "fix" unrelated failures; run the scoped test files instead.
- Never hard-code connection strings or Okta values; they come from user secrets / environment variables.
- Database columns are discovered, not guessed. For `SpruceMetrics` use the `mssql-readonly` MCP before writing a mapper.
